From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:12:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: stop repeated deterministic tool input failures

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Stop repeated deterministic panel and applet input errors
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-fix
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 0002-candidate-add-hook-context-and-post-tool-transform.patch
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 1010-personal-fix-stop-repeated-deterministic-tool-input-failures.patch

Patch intent:
Stop a turn after three matching typed deterministic tool-input failures,
including unknown tool names and nested batch dispatches, in both turn loops.
Preserve exact matching for uncategorized errors and use stable panel and applet
input categories so revised arguments can reach correction without extra
provider retries.

Why it exists:
Repeated invalid inputs can otherwise trigger repeated provider requests without
progress. Classification is explicit through a typed error, not inferred from
error text. Panel and applet deterministic input failures are categorized;
unknown tool names are typed but uncategorized. Runtime and other untyped tool
errors remain unclassified.

Upstream integration points:
The change extends tool::retry_guard and wraps Registry::execute dispatches,
including nested BatchTool calls. Agent::run_turn and
Agent::run_turn_streaming_mpsc reset and check the shared per-turn guard.
PanelTool and AppletTool expose UI schemas and validate their inputs; OpenAI
strict-schema normalization requires nullable panel fields while dynamic applet
node fields remain non-strict. Registry also types unknown tool names. The retry
guard depends on hook context established by patch 0002.

Update guidance:
Keep failure classification limited to explicit typed input errors and unknown
tool names. Preserve exact matching for uncategorized errors, stable categories
for panel and applet input failures, tool/category separation, and clearing
matching prior failures after a successful call. Keep runtime failures untyped.
Preserve cloned-registry guard state, nested batch dispatch tracking, the
bounded repeat window, and terminal checks in both turn loops. Keep the UI tool
schemas aligned with their deserializers and preserve permissive nested applet
fields.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-app-core panel --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core applet --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core retry_guard --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core malformed_tool_call_recovery_tests --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core tool::batch_tests --lib
